  "attempt": "Let tau be an involution of a finite set and w>=0 a baseline. For R_N(f)=sum_a f(a)f(tau(a)), the exact squared L2 distance from w to the nonnegative endpoint-hole set {f:R_N(f)=0} is rho_N(w)^2=sum over two-cycles {a,b} of min(w(a)^2,w(b)^2), plus sum over fixed points a of w(a)^2. Thus ||f-w||_2^2<rho_N(w)^2 forces R_N(f)>0, and equality is sharp. However, endpoint positivity is not determined by any permutation-invariant global moments: on Z/4 at N=3, (2s,s,0,0) and (2s,0,0,s) have the same multiset and every global power moment, while their endpoint convolutions are 0 and 4s^2.",
